  "discussion": "The ridge of high pressure over the southeast will continue to weaken, but temperatures will still rise into the mid to upper 90s this afternoon from the lower Mississippi Valley north through Tennessee. Relative humidity will bottom out near 25-30% again today as well. In the Pacific Northwest, a trough aloft will bring breezy west winds gusting to 25 mph to cascade gaps and relative humidity will fall to 15-30% again this afternoon east of the Cascades. Further south, slightly above average temperatures are expected across northern California today along with breezy overnight winds and poor relative humidity recovery after RH falls to 10-20% this afternoon. Isolated mixed wet and dry thunderstorms will develop this afternoon across southern and western Nevada including across the Sierra Front. Isolated thunderstorms will also develop across the lower Mississippi Valley and across west Texas today, bring gusty outflow winds with them. Conditions trend drier across the desert southwest, though high temperatures remain mostly below normal. Today will be the driest day of the week across the southern Front Range with relative humidity dropping into the teens."
 },
